    "note": "Field uniform: the removable rectangular sleeve (pogonchik tipa 'mufta') of the jacket's camouflage cloth, no button, no lumen, no piping; stripes and stars in protective colour (Ukaz 293 field-uniform wording, Prikaz MO 525: 'pogony s'emnye, pryamougol'nye'; the GUSP 48/2009 analogue confirms protective colour for stars and stripes). Medium (official-text extracts): narrow stripes 10 mm, wide 30 mm (Ukaz 531/293); stars 13 mm for junior officers and praporshchiki (Ukaz 293); a pair 'midway between the centre line and the edge' (+-12.5 mm on a 50 mm board); arrangements per rank. Medium-low (one extract each, not reproduced): first stripe 25 mm from the shoulder end on field-jacket boards with 2 mm gaps (Prikaz 525 table 3); first star centre 25 mm from that end, rows 25 mm apart (table 1); starshina's wide stripe running along the board. Low: the board's size (50 x 120 mm, retail), its square ends, the hex colours (camouflage drawn as one olive, devices dark olive). Presentation only: below 40 px tall (card rows) the devices are drawn darker with a light 1 px outline so they read. Search extracts only; no page could be opened."
